Stop the HID poll tick from using a device while it is closed and freed.

The tick (every 4 ms, on the timer thread) takes a snapshot of the open devices, then calls
each one's poll() with the device lock held. A close on another thread (Steam's CloseDevice on
the session thread, or the tick's own close of a device that failed) marked the device closed
and freed it without taking that lock, so a tick that already had its snapshot went on into
freed memory: poll() writes the device's state and report buffer, and the lock itself is read
through device->managed, which the close had cleared. On a heap that shows up later and
elsewhere, as a corrupted free list in an unrelated malloc.

IHS_HIDManagedDeviceClose now marks the device closed under the device lock, and the tick
checks the flag under the same lock before it calls poll(). Once the close has let go of the
lock no tick is inside the device or can enter it, so the free that follows is safe. A second
close of the same device (the tick and Steam both closing it) finds the flag set and returns.

diff --git a/src/hid/device.c b/src/hid/device.c
index adf987a..190503a 100644
--- a/src/hid/device.c
+++ b/src/hid/device.c
@@ -42,11 +42,20 @@ void IHS_HIDManagedDeviceOpened(IHS_HIDManagedDevice *managed) {
 
 void IHS_HIDManagedDeviceClose(IHS_HIDManagedDevice *managed) {
     assert(managed != NULL);
-    IHS_HIDDevice *device = managed->device;
     assert(managed->manager != NULL);
+    // The poll tick runs poll() with this lock held and skips closed devices. Marking the device
+    // closed under the lock means no tick is inside it, or can enter it, once the lock is let go.
+    // A second close (the tick closing a dead device, Steam closing it too) finds it closed.
+    IHS_MutexLock(managed->lock);
+    if (managed->closed) {
+        IHS_MutexUnlock(managed->lock);
+        return;
+    }
+    IHS_HIDManagerRemoveClosedDevice(managed->manager, managed);
+    IHS_MutexUnlock(managed->lock);
+    IHS_HIDDevice *device = managed->device;
     device->cls->close(device);
     IHS_HIDManagerNotifyDeviceClosed(managed->manager, managed);
-    IHS_HIDManagerRemoveClosedDevice(managed->manager, managed);
     device->managed = NULL;
     device->cls->free(device);
 }
